    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is centered around **Tyler Freeman** (72.80) and **Matt Chapman** (69.71). **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a prime matchup against a mediocre arm in Sandy Alcantara, with park factors fueling a significant boost to his base projection. Meanwhile, **Matt Chapman** is our most compelling play; despite the platoon disadvantage against Eduardo Rodriguez, he is elevated by an elite BvP history (29 PA) and a \"Slow SP\" designation that effectively weaponizes his stolen base potential, compounded by the value of leading off. **Dylan Beavers** (66.63) also warrants attention as a high-upside play, leveraging a strong park factor and a favorable matchup against Sean Burke to anchor the lower half of our outfield production.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our bench, where **Daulton Varsho** (41.75) was the final exclusion. While **Daulton Varsho** maintains a respectable floor, he is hampered by a significant negative adjustment due to Sean Manaea\u2019s skill set and a platoon disadvantage that renders him less efficient than our current starters. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, while **Masyn Winn** is held out today due to a lack of a scheduled contest. As we wait for official lineups, please note that **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Luis Arraez**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Bryson Stott**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Matt Chapman**, **Lawrence Butler**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Taylor Ward**, and **Gavin Sheets** are currently projected based on historical batting order assumptions; any unexpected shifts in the lineup cards may necessitate a reassessment of our efficiency scores before first pitch.",
